<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>Ahjo.Vulkan.Ngx.Tests</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>Ahjo.Vulkan.Ngx.Tests</AssemblyName>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <IsTestProject>true</IsTestProject>
    <AllowUnsafeBlocks>true</AllowUnsafeBlocks>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="xunit.v3" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\Ahjo.Vulkan.Ngx\Ahjo.Vulkan.Ngx.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    Most of this suite needs no device: shadow-enum drift, description
    validation, the extension-copy contract and the AhjoValidation-gated
    evaluate checks all run on a bare runner. But some tests DO create a
    VkDevice, which makes this a suite that touches Vulkan — so it carries the
    declared-tier contract like the other four that do (issue #158,
    docs/ci-coverage.md), and every skip goes through
    Ahjo.Vulkan.Testing.TestGate rather than a bare Assert.Skip.

    Two gate classes, both permanent-and-correct rather than coverage gaps:
      [gate:platform] — the ahjo_ngx shim is not staged (DLSS is opt-in;
                        ./tools/setup-ngx.ps1).
      [gate:feature]  — no NVIDIA GPU with a DLSS-capable driver and a
                        consumer-supplied nvngx_dlss.dll.
    Neither needs a ci.yml edit: both classes already exist.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Include="..\Shared\*.cs" LinkBase="Shared" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
